# Build output
/bin/
/rendezvous
frontend/dist/

# build/ is NOT ignored wholesale: it also holds committed packaging inputs the
# release needs (appicon.svg, windows/icon.ico, windows/installer.nsi,
# versioninfo.json — see scripts/publish-release.sh). Only the generated
# subtrees go: wails output, and the patched libc module fork `make
# android-core` materializes.
/build/bin/
/build/libc-fork/

# Node
frontend/node_modules/

# Local multi-peer test data (make peers)
/.dev/

# Wails
/frontend/wailsjs/
dist-release/
resource_windows_amd64.syso

# Twemoji assets, copied from node_modules by `npm run prep-twemoji`
frontend/public/twemoji/

# Coding-agent state (sessions, worktrees, local settings, skills) is
# per-machine and per-person, and none of it is documentation a contributor
# should have to know to look for. What was worth keeping out of .claude/skills/
# lives in CONTRIBUTING.md instead, under the multi-peer dev loop.
/.claude/

# Bundled meme templates: third-party images with real rightsholders. Kept out
# of the repo so nothing here redistributes them; drop your own pack in this
# directory and the editor picks it up at runtime. The README is the exception
# and IS tracked — it carries the provenance and licensing position, and three
# other documents cite it, so ignoring it left those citations pointing at
# nothing for anyone who had not run prep-memes.mjs.
# The pattern excludes the directory's CONTENTS, not the directory: git cannot
# re-include a file whose parent directory is itself excluded, so `memes/` plus
# a negation would silently keep ignoring the README.
frontend/public/memes/*
!frontend/public/memes/README.md
